# The build context is the repository root. See src/Xakpc.SQLiteMCPSidecar/Dockerfile.
#
# The image needs global.json, Directory.Build.props and src/ only. Everything else stays out, thus
# a dev database or a lode change does not send bytes to the daemon and does not invalidate a layer.

# Build output. Directory.Build.props sends every project here, and build/dev/ holds the dev
# database and its backups. The bin and obj rules do not cover it.
build/
TestResults/

**/bin
**/obj

# Not part of the image.
test/
scripts/
docs/
.lode/
.github/

# Source control and editors.
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.vs
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/*.user
**/*.suo

# Secrets and local configuration. A context that carries a token is a token that reaches a layer.
**/.env
**/secrets.dev.yaml
**/values.dev.yaml
**/*.pfx

# Container definitions. The daemon reads them over its own path, not from the context.
**/Dockerfile*
**/.dockerignore
compose*.yaml
compose*.yml
docker-compose*

**/node_modules
